Hi team,

The resilience plan lists systems, but customers experience end-to-end servic=
es that cross ATM, card, transaction and communication processes.

We looked at a version of this before. For the March 2020 review, please show=
 what changed and whether the earlier conclusion still holds. Failure anecdot=
es are beginning to drive decisions, although retries and late posting may be=
 making the problem look larger than the affected-customer population.

Can you test these explanations rather than choosing one at the start?
- manual workarounds create later reconciliation breaks
- recovery restores authorisation before posting catches up
- cash access degrades before account servicing

The decision is the order in which critical services should be recovered and =
tested. Please give us a Power BI page with drill-through to a reproducible c=
ase list.

You should be able to build the evidence from transaction-level timestamps, c=
hannels, amounts, statuses and error context; ATM attempts, host responses, P=
IN attempts, blocked-card state and latency; customer contacts, complaints an=
d suggestions; debit-order mandates, collection dates, suspensions and cancel=
lations. Treat this as a historical service-impact rehearsal, not proof of in=
frastructure capacity.

Thanks
